      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a profound and terrifying emptiness, and it's okay to feel completely lost right now. That feeling of being an echo, a shadow, is a natural response when the anchor of your life is suddenly gone. You don't have to rebuild who you were; you can simply let go of the need to be anything at all. Sometimes, the quietest, most immediate act of self-compassion is just letting the pain be real, and finding a very small, quiet way to take care of that emptiness.",
